  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{機|き} (machine, mechanism) + {能|のう} (ability, capability). Literally \"the ability of a mechanism.\"\n\nUSAGE:\nAs a する verb, {機能|きのう}する means \"to function\" or \"to work.\" Often used in negative contexts: {機能|きのう}しない (doesn't function), {機能|きのう}していない (is not functioning). Note the homophone {昨日|きのう} (yesterday), which has a completely different meaning.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {機能|きのう}する: to function, to work\n- {機能|きのう}が{低下|ていか}する: function declines\n- {機能|きのう}を{果|は}たす: to fulfill a function\n- {機能|きのう}を{追加|ついか}する: to add a feature\n- {高機能|こうきのう}: high-performance, feature-rich\n- {多機能|たきのう}: multifunctional",
